{
  "id": "competitive-langmuir-closed-sorption-environment",
  "name": "Closed competitive Langmuir sorption to a finite shared surface",
  "category": "environment",
  "description": "Two solutes compete for one finite set of noninteracting sites in a closed well-mixed batch. Site vacancy is capacity minus the two sorbed inventories; each aqueous-plus-sorbed solute total is conserved. Equal single-site occupancy and ideal mass-action rates are assumptions, not a calibrated contaminant isotherm. This is a finite-reservoir extension of the elementary Langmuir law, not copied source code. All numerical parameters, initial values, horizon and solver settings are illustrative teaching choices; not fitted to a field site. Signed net-rate flows encode state equations, not material transport claims. No numerical clipping or arbitrary domain clamps.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1021/ja02242a004",
  "reference": "Langmuir(1918), The adsorption of gases on plane surfaces of glass, mica and platinum, JACS40:1361-1403. Reversible site-occupancy law applied here to an explicitly specified finite aqueous batch.",
